WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.024 --> 00:00:02.670
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.140
- [Narrator] Located in
the town of Patan, in India

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.170
is a 90-foot-deep stepwell,
with an even deeper

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.998
connection to the past.

00:00:09.998 --> 00:00:12.581
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.270
Built inside an opening in the ground,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.220
approximately 200 feet
long and 65 feet wide,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.890
the stepwell is designed as a
seven level, inverted temple.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.820
Throughout history, most
monuments have been constructed

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.640
by men with the intention
of honoring their wives.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.240
However, Rani ki vav is different

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.760
as it was initially built
as a memorial to the king

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.810
in the 11th century AD, by his wife.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.360
Hence, it became known
as the Queen's Stepwell.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.090
In the past stepwells were
common throughout India.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.810
These wells were primarily
used to collect water.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.730
However, they also became
a place of socializing

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.780
and an important aspect of the community

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.070
to people of the time.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.800
It features more than
500 principle sculptures

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.170
and at least 1,000 smaller sculptures,

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.650
all in religious or mythological imagery.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.930
At the trend's peak, there were

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.080
roughly 3,000 stepwells in India.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.180
However, today, only around 1,000 remain.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.260
Rani ki vav serves as a
valuable visual history

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.130
to teach and remind visitors

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.147
about the traditions of the past.

00:01:18.147 --> 00:01:20.647
(light music)

00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:26.833
(ringing music)

